        </script><script data-n-head="true" type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://www.fox4news.com/election/denton-county-voting-locations-wait-times-sample-ballots#webpage","url":"https://www.fox4news.com/election/denton-county-voting-locations-wait-times-sample-ballots","name":"Denton County voting locations, wait times & sample ballots","description":"Tuesday is election day in Texas! Here are the locations where you can cast your ballot in Denton County for the Nov. 3 election.","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://www.fox4news.com/#website"},"mainEntity":{"@id":"https://www.fox4news.com/election/denton-county-voting-locations-wait-times-sample-ballots#article"},"breadcrumb":{"@id":"https://www.fox4news.com/election/denton-county-voting-locations-wait-times-sample-ballots#breadcrumb"},"primaryImageOfPage":{"@id":"https://www.fox4news.com/election/denton-county-voting-locations-wait-times-sample-ballots#primaryimage"}},{"@type":"NewsArticle","@id":"https://www.fox4news.com/election/denton-county-voting-locations-wait-times-sample-ballots#article","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://www.fox4news.com/election/denton-county-voting-locations-wait-times-sample-ballots#webpage"},"headline":"Denton County voting locations, wait times & sample ballots","name":"Denton County voting locations, wait times & sample ballots","description":"Tuesday is election day in Texas! Here are the locations where you can cast your ballot in Denton County for the Nov. 3 election.","articleSection":"Election","datePublished":"2026-11-03T06:00:42-06:00","dateModified":"2026-11-02T11:43:21-06:00","author":[{"@id":"https://fox4news.com/person/m/grace-marocco#person","@type":"Person","name":"Grace Marocco","url":"https://fox4news.com/person/m/grace-marocco"}],"publisher":{"@id":"https://www.fox4news.com/#organization"},"image":{"@id":"https://www.fox4news.com/election/denton-county-voting-locations-wait-times-sample-ballots#primaryimage"},"mainEntityOfPage":{"@id":"https://www.fox4news.com/election/denton-county-voting-locations-wait-times-sample-ballots#webpage"},"articleBody":"Tuesday is election day in Texas!Voting for the Nov. 3 General and Joint Election runs from 7 a.m. to 7 p.m.Here&apos;s where to cast your ballot in Denton County, and other important things to know before you head to the polls.&#xA0;Denton County registered voters should vote at their specific precinct polling locations.&#xA0;To find a voting center that&apos;s near you, visit the&#xA0;Denton County Voting Center Finder. All voting centers and their addresses are listed in the document below.If you have questions about your ballot, voting locations, or anything else, ask your county election office.&#xA0;Anderson County&#xA0;|&#xA0;Bosque County&#xA0;|&#xA0;Collin County&#xA0;|&#xA0;Cooke County&#xA0;|&#xA0;Dallas County&#xA0;|&#xA0;Delta County&#xA0;|&#xA0;Denton County&#xA0;|&#xA0;Ellis County&#xA0;|&#xA0;Erath County&#xA0;|&#xA0;Fannin County&#xA0;|&#xA0;Freestone County&#xA0;|&#xA0;Henderson County&#xA0;|&#xA0;Hill County&#xA0;|&#xA0;Hood County&#xA0;|&#xA0;Hopkins County&#xA0;|&#xA0;Hunt County&#xA0;|&#xA0;Jack County&#xA0;|&#xA0;Johnson County&#xA0;|&#xA0;Kaufman County&#xA0;|&#xA0;Lamar County&#xA0;|&#xA0;Navarro County&#xA0;|&#xA0;Palo Pinto County&#xA0;|&#xA0;Parker County&#xA0;|&#xA0;Rains County&#xA0;|&#xA0;Red River County&#xA0;|&#xA0;Rockwall County&#xA0;|&#xA0;Somervell County&#xA0;|&#xA0;Tarrant County&#xA0;|&#xA0;Van Zandt County&#xA0;|&#xA0;Wise CountyIf you have more questions about the voting process, you can find more information here.&#xA0;Denton County does not post its wait times online.The state&apos;s most high profile race involves Ken Paxton (R) and James Talarico (D), who are vying for a spot in the U.S. Senate. Paxton, who has served as Texas Attorney General since 2014, unseated sitting Sen. John Cornyn in the Republican primary. Talarico, a former middle school teacher and Presbyterian seminarian, has served in the Texas House since 2018, and defeated U.S. Rep. Jasmine Crockett in the Democratic primary.The&#xA0;FOX 4 Elections&#xA0;page also has breakdowns of some of the hot ticket items Texans are voting on during this election.The easiest way to check your voter registration status is to head to the Secretary of State&apos;s website. The Am I Registered portal on the website lets you submit your identifying information, like a Texas Driver&apos;s License number or details about your birth. You will find out instantly if you&apos;re registered to vote. The portal will also give your poll locations.&#xA0;The polls in Denton County are open from 7 a.m. on the date of the election until 7 p.m. Anyone in line at the time the polls close will be allowed to cast their ballot.&#xA0;In order to vote in person on election day, Texas voters will be asked to present an acceptable form of photo ID. Here is list of the acceptable forms of photo ID:Here is a list of the supporting forms of ID that can be presented if the voter does not possess an acceptable form of photo identification and cannot reasonably obtain one:&#xA0;For more information on acceptable forms of ID and what you can do if you do not have one,&#xA0;click here.If you have a form of acceptable photo ID and are between the ages of 18 and 69, your ID must be current or expired for no more than 4 years to qualify to vote. For voters 70 and older, your photo ID can be expired for any length of time if the identification is otherwise okay.According to the&#xA0;U.S. government, you can bring notes or a sample ballot with you to the polls. In Texas, polling locations restrict cell phone use.&#xA0;No. Only peace officers - on our off duty - can take a handgun into a polling location.&#xA0;Yes, and no. You cannot use your cell phone, camera, tablet, laptop, sound recorder or any other kind of recording device in the room where voting is happening. You can use electronic devices outside the room, as long as you are not using them to record sound or images. No recording is allowed within 100 feet of a voting station.No. No one is allowed to wear clothing or any similar items related to a candidate, measure, or political party, even if they are not on the ballot. This is enforceable within 100 feet of a polling station. You will be asked to remove or cover up the clothing before entering the building.Yes, according to&#xA0;Texas Election Code, a child under 18 years old can accompany a parent who is voting.If you have problems or questions, you can call the Secretary of State&#x2019;s toll-free election hotline at 1-800-252-VOTE (8683) or email&#xA0;elections@sos.texas.gov.&#xA0;To file a formal complaint,&#xA0;download the complaint form here. It can be submitted by mail, fax, or email.","url":"https://www.fox4news.com/election/denton-county-voting-locations-wait-times-sample-ballots","isAccessibleForFree":true,"keywords":"elections-2026,tx-politics,politics,election,denton-county"},{"@type":"ImageObject","@id":"https://www.fox4news.com/election/denton-county-voting-locations-wait-times-sample-ballots#primaryimage","url":"https://static.fox4news.com/www.fox4news.com/content/uploads/2026/02/denton-where-to-vote.jpg"},{"@type":"Person","@id":"https://fox4news.com/person/m/grace-marocco#person","name":"Grace Marocco","url":"https://fox4news.com/person/m/grace-marocco","jobTitle":"Dallas Digital Content Creator","worksFor":{"@id":"https://www.fox4news.com/#organization"}},{"@type":"NewsMediaOrganization","@id":"https://www.fox4news.com/#organization","name":"FOX 4 Dallas-Fort Worth","alternateName":"KDFW, FOX 4, FOX 4 Dallas-Fort Worth","url":"https://www.fox4news.com/","sameAs":["https://www.facebook.com/Fox4DFW/","https://twitter.com/FOX4","https://www.instagram.com/fox4news/","https://www.youtube.com/fox4news/","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/KDFW","",""],"foundingDate":"1949-12-03","logo":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://static.foxtv.com/static/orion/img/kdfw/favicons/favico